{"id":176596598263797,"type":"album","name":"A Wizard, a True Star","artist":"Todd Rundgren","year":1973,"weight":21,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710603.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-13f8dfa4-c630-4cb7-879b-755db7dba640/mbid-13f8dfa4-c630-4cb7-879b-755db7dba640-23167890008.png","yt":"iEIi4lj-ISQ","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/todd-rundgren/a-wizard-a-true-star"},"desc":"Something/Anything? proved that Todd Rundgren could write a pop classic as gracefully as any of his peers, but buried beneath the surface were signs that he would never be satisfied as merely a pop singer/songwriter. A close listen to the album reveals the eccentricities and restless spirit that surges to the forefront on its follow-up, A Wizard, A True Star. Anyone expecting the third record of Something/Anything?, filled with variations on \"I Saw the Light\" and \"Hello It's Me,\" will be shocked by A Wizard. As much a mind-f*ck as an album, A Wizard, A True Star rarely breaks down ."},"artist_ref":{"id":155463229665045,"name":"Todd Rundgren","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/ToddRundgren.png?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":191826593279813,"type":"genre","name":"Art Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":531,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":138197775829889,"type":"genre","name":"Progressive Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":439,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":51891856250504,"type":"genre","name":"Proto-Punk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":71,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":55893123468232,"type":"genre","name":"Experimental Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":373,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":126030611694007,"type":"genre","name":"Art Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":310,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":141164231500862,"type":"genre","name":"Psychedelic Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":245,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":132119653572823,"type":"genre","name":"Progressive Pop","artist":null,"ye